# S27 (SKOS Reference 8.4): skos:related is disjoint with the
# property skos:broaderTransitive. broaderTransitive is rarely
# asserted directly (skos:broader is its usual, unmaterialized,
# sub-property) so this variant walks the transitive closure of
# skos:broader with a property path instead of requiring an OWL-RL
# pass first. Checks both directions because skos:related is
# symmetric in the SKOS model but that symmetry is also usually
# left to entailment rather than asserted twice in the data.
# Run: factoidal query --data DATA.ttl --query THIS.rq
PREFIX skos: <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#>
ASK {
  ?a skos:related ?b .
  { ?a skos:broader+ ?b } UNION { ?b skos:broader+ ?a }
}
